§§ `Schedule 1 Part 2 -- the stages of a damages claim (2024-25, $124.53 a unit)`

-- Settled for $30,000 without a certificate, liability admitted: stages 1 and 2, 7.24 units; stage 3(c), 7.24 units and
-- 12 cents a dollar over $20,000 ($1,200): 14.48 units = $1,803.1944, plus $1,200 = $3,003.19, $3,003.
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE FALSE `resolved without a certificate of claims assessment` TRUE 30000 FALSE 0 0 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 3003
-- $15,000, liability not admitted: 7.24 units ($901.60) plus 10 cents a dollar ($1,500) = $2,401.60, $2,402.
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE FALSE `resolved without a certificate of claims assessment` FALSE 15000 FALSE 0 0 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 2402
-- $20,000 exactly, admitted: 14.48 units, $1,803; $20,001: 12 cents more, still $1,803.
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE FALSE `resolved without a certificate of claims assessment` TRUE 20000 FALSE 0 0 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 1803
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE FALSE `resolved without a certificate of claims assessment` TRUE 20001 FALSE 0 0 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 1803
-- Settled after a $200,000 assessment, admitted: stage 4 = stage 3(g) on $200,000 (114.48 units + $2,000) plus 2 cents a
-- dollar ($4,000): 121.72 units ($15,157.79) + $6,000 = $21,157.79, $21,158.
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE FALSE `resolved after a certificate of claims assessment, without court proceedings` TRUE 200000 FALSE 0 200000 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 21158
-- After court: assessment $80,000, not admitted; award $150,000 less $30,000 weekly benefits = $120,000. Stage 3(f) on
-- $80,000: 71.28 units + $3,000; stage 4 adds $1,600; stage 5 adds $2,400. 78.52 units ($9,778.10) + $7,000 =
-- $16,778.10, $16,778.
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE FALSE `finalised after court proceedings began` FALSE 150000 TRUE 30000 80000 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 16778
-- Table B (retained after the certificate): $60,000: 3.56 + 37.8 units ($5,150.56) + 8 cents x $10,000 = $5,950.56,
-- $5,951; $20,000: 3.56 units, $443.33, $443; $30,000: $443.33 + $1,000, $1,443.
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE TRUE `resolved after a certificate of claims assessment, without court proceedings` TRUE 60000 FALSE 0 55000 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 5951
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE TRUE `finalised after court proceedings began` TRUE 20000 FALSE 0 15000 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 443
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` FALSE TRUE `finalised after court proceedings began` TRUE 30000 FALSE 0 15000 `in 2024-25` EQUALS JUST 1443
#ASSERT `What is the most my lawyer may charge for my damages claim` TRUE FALSE `finalised after court proceedings began` TRUE 30000 FALSE 0 15000 `in 2024-25` EQUALS NOTHING

